Lock an authz only after reading its order and account

The Authz handler held the authz write lock while it read the order and
looked up the account, which takes the store's read lock, and
updateChallenge read the order under the authz read lock. The store takes
authz locks under its own lock (FindValidAuthorization, on every new
order) and under the order's (GetOrderByID), so once a writer queues on
the store or the order, an authz poll, a new order or a read of the
authz's order, and that writer wait on each other and the CA stops
answering. Read the order and the account first, then lock the authz only
to change or render it.
